[{"id":2837256083,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6pHReT","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?u=f7f8e0273f784f5ec6f6b7fe4a88d449896eb48a&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","login":"Ivorforce","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce"},"body":"Thanks! This makes sense to me in principle.\r\n\r\nHowever, simply moving a function from one header to another isn't a worthy goal in and of itself (even if the target header is a better fit). To motivate this PR better, it would be nice to show an improvement of speed, and / or de-duplication of code.\r\n\r\nWe also have a PR open which optimizes `bisect` functionality in a few spots (https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/90036, cc @nazarwadim). The improvement seems to be mostly using uniformly unsigned types, so this is worth a look. \r\nPerhaps it would be possible to de-duplicate some of the implementations https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/90036, with the `Span` based one? At least, if there's no regression of performance, this would be nice.\r\n","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106357#pullrequestreview-2837256083","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106357","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-05-13T15:34:25Z"},{"id":2839035727,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6pOD9P","state":"APPROVED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?u=f7f8e0273f784f5ec6f6b7fe4a88d449896eb48a&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","login":"Ivorforce","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce"},"body":"Between a little optimization and deduplication, I think this PR is now better motivated. Thanks!\r\n\r\nYour commits seem logical, but I think one commit suffices for the complexity of this change, so a squash may be in order. Besides that, I'd just like to propose storing `bisect` not as `int`, even if `int` is returned later anyway, just to offload the loss of range to as late as possible.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106357#pullrequestreview-2839035727","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106357","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-05-14T08:00:56Z"},{"id":2839605060,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6pQO9E","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67693830?u=5127cb92ac85d3db01550c026a62da13254bd17e&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/YYF233333","id":67693830,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NjkzODMw","login":"YYF233333","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106357#pullrequestreview-2839605060","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106357","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2025-05-14T10:14:12Z"},{"id":2839757445,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6pQ0KF","state":"APPROVED","commit_id":"3bf400ffaea9301e7737f5b51d566c88d9ac9b63","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?u=f7f8e0273f784f5ec6f6b7fe4a88d449896eb48a&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-0